# ============================================================
# CLICKFUD — Paystack payment secrets
#
# These are NOT loaded from a .env file at runtime — Supabase Edge
# Functions read secrets from the platform's own secret store, set with:
#
#   supabase secrets set PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_xxxxx --project-ref ctxnwjjpqxecidzblyok
#
# or via the Dashboard: Project Settings -> Edge Functions -> Secrets.
# This file exists only as a reference for what needs to be set, with no
# real values — never commit real keys anywhere in this repository.
# ============================================================

# The only Paystack secret this app needs. Server-side only — read by
# paystack-initialize, paystack-verify, paystack-webhook,
# paystack-charge-saved, paystack-cancel-order, paystack-manage-subaccount,
# paystack-list-banks. Never sent to the browser in any response.
#
# Its own prefix IS the mode — Paystack does not have a separate "mode"
# setting to configure. There is deliberately no PAYSTACK_MODE variable
# here: inventing one would just duplicate what this key's prefix already
# says, and could drift out of sync with the actual key in use.
#   sk_test_...  -> TEST mode (no real money moves)
#   sk_live_...  -> LIVE mode (real money moves) — only set this once
#                   Paystack has approved the account for the payment
#                   channels you need (see the setup guide).
PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=

# There is no separate Paystack "public key" secret needed here. This
# app never embeds Paystack.js or collects card details in the browser —
# every payment goes through a server-initiated Checkout redirect
# (paystack-initialize returns a Paystack-hosted authorization_url), so a
# client-side public key is never required. If a future feature ever DOES
# need Paystack.js inline (not currently the case), that key is safe to
# expose client-side by design — it is not a secret — and would be read
# from js/config.js, not from here.

# There is no separate "webhook secret" either. Unlike some other payment
# providers, Paystack signs webhooks with the SAME secret key above
# (HMAC-SHA512 over the raw request body, sent as the x-paystack-signature
# header) — see paystack-webhook/index.ts. Nothing extra to configure here.

# SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are
# provided automatically by the Supabase Edge Runtime for every function —
# never set these manually as secrets.
